    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Growth</span> is the permanent, irreversible increase in the size, mass, and complexity of a living organism. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Irritability</span> (also called sensitivity) is the ability to detect changes (stimuli) in the environment and make appropriate responses. Both are fundamental life processes that enable organisms to survive and adapt.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning and Processes of Growth</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Growth at the cellular level involves three processes:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Cell division (mitosis):</strong> Increases the number of cells in the organism</li>\n  <li><strong>Cell enlargement:</strong> Each new cell increases in size by taking in water and synthesizing more cytoplasm</li>\n  <li><strong>Cell differentiation:</strong> Cells develop specialized structures and functions (e.g., nerve cells, muscle cells)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Importance of Growth</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Enables organisms to mature and reproduce</li>\n  <li>Allows repair and replacement of damaged or worn-out tissues</li>\n  <li>Provides increased body mass for survival</li>\n  <li>Leads to differentiation and specialization for efficient functioning</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Measurement of Growth</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Growth can be measured by changes in:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Height or length</strong> — simple but may fluctuate</li>\n  <li><strong>Wet mass</strong> — affected by water content (not always reliable)</li>\n  <li><strong>Dry mass</strong> — most accurate measure (removes water effect); kills the organism</li>\n  <li><strong>Cell number</strong> — counted under microscope</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Irritability: Meaning and Processes</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Irritability involves two steps: <strong>reception</strong> (detecting the stimulus) and <strong>response</strong> (reacting to it).</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Organism</th><th>Stimulus</th><th>Response</th><th>Name</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Plant shoot</td><td>Light</td><td>Bends toward light</td><td>Phototropism</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Plant root</td><td>Gravity</td><td>Grows downward</td><td>Geotropism</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Plant root</td><td>Water</td><td>Grows toward water</td><td>Hydrotropism</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Amoeba</td><td>Chemical (food)</td><td>Moves toward it</td><td>Positive chemotaxis</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Animal</td><td>Pain</td><td>Withdraws from stimulus</td><td>Reflex action</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Importance of Irritability</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Enables organisms to detect and avoid danger</li>\n  <li>Helps locate food sources</li>\n  <li>Allows plants to position leaves for maximum photosynthesis</li>\n  <li>Coordinates bodily functions through the nervous and endocrine systems</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Dry mass is the most reliable measure of growth because wet mass varies with water content. A seed losing water during germination might show a decrease in wet mass but an increase in dry mass as new organic molecules are synthesized.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Growth is a permanent increase in size/mass through cell division (mitosis), cell enlargement, and differentiation. Best measured as dry mass. Irritability is the ability to detect stimuli and respond. Plant tropisms (phototropism, geotropism, hydrotropism) and animal reflexes are examples. Both growth and irritability are essential life processes for survival.\n</div>\n  ",
